      content: '**Immediate Response — Take the Statement Seriously**:\n\n\"I appreciate you trusting me with how you are feeling. What you just said about your family being better off without you — I want to make sure I understand what you mean. Are you having thoughts of ending your life or harming yourself?\"\n\n**If he endorses suicidal ideation, assess further using the Columbia Suicide Severity Rating Scale (C-SSRS) framework**:\n1. **Ideation**: \"Have you actually been thinking about killing yourself?\" (Active vs. passive ideation)\n2. **Plan**: \"Have you thought about how you would do it?\"\n3. **Intent**: \"Do you have any intention of acting on these thoughts?\"\n4. **Means**: \"Do you have access to firearms, medications, or other means?\" (Amputees have increased access to prescription medications)\n5. **Preparatory behaviors**: \"Have you done anything to prepare, like giving away possessions or writing notes?\"\n6. **Protective factors**: \"What has kept you from acting on these thoughts?\" (Family, faith, fear of consequences)\n\n**Risk Factors Present in This Patient**:\n- Male sex (higher completion rate)\n- Chronic pain\n- Recent major disability/amputation\n- Loss of independence and role identity\n- Social isolation (stopped attending church)\n- Hopelessness\n- Depression (likely — needs formal screening)\n\n**Management Based on Risk Level**:\n\n**If imminent risk (active plan with intent and means)**:\n- Do not leave the patient alone\n- Activate emergency psychiatric evaluation (call 988 Suicide and Crisis Lifeline or 911)\n- Means restriction counseling (secure medications, firearms)\n\n**If moderate risk (ideation without imminent plan)**:\n- Administer PHQ-9 formally (score likely elevated)\n- Initiate antidepressant: **sertraline 50 mg daily** (safe with his cardiac history)\n- Urgent referral to psychiatry or psychology within 1-2 weeks\n- Establish a **safety plan** (Stanley-Brown Safety Planning): identify warning signs, coping strategies, people to contact, crisis resources\n- Provide crisis numbers: **988 Suicide and Crisis Lifeline**, Crisis Text Line (text HOME to 741741)\n\n**Regardless of Risk Level — Address Isolation and Peer Support**:\n\"I want to connect you with people who understand exactly what you are going through. There is an amputee support group that meets at our hospital every other Thursday. Many of the members felt exactly like you do now, and they have found ways to rebuild meaningful lives. Would you be willing to try one meeting?\"\n\n**Additional resources**: Amputee Coalition of America peer support network, online forums, recreational therapy programs, adaptive sports programs.\n\n**Follow-up**: Schedule a return visit within 1-2 weeks. Document suicide risk assessment thoroughly. Communicate with PCP and any mental health providers. Consider involving the patient\'s wife in a future session to address caregiver burden and relationship dynamics.\n\n**Key principles demonstrated**: Direct and compassionate suicide screening, structured risk assessment, evidence-based intervention, crisis resource provision, peer support engagement, coordinated follow-up.',
